{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1008527-skills-for-agriculture","id":1008527,"title":"Skills for agriculture?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-26T07:36:50-08:00","id":1008527,"title":"Skills for agriculture?","content":"I thinking about running <b>Dark Eras</b> <i>Sundered World</i> story - and then farming is one of most important part of life in setting. Playing common farmer is valid character concept. What would by your advice Skills for farmer character?<br /> <br /> I think that Animal Ken is obvious. Crops farming would be under Survival and Science, yes? Anything else to choose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-26-2016, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T08:12:48-08:00","id":1008542,"title":"","content":"I'd also go with athletics for the more physical part of farming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T08:53:20-08:00","id":1008565,"title":"","content":"As I've explained in an earlier thread I really don't think Survival has much to do with plants, except for recognizing edible plants in the wild.<br /> <br /> Science seems the most logical choice for farming crops since it requires detailed knowledge of when and how you need to sow your crops, knowing to fertilize them, knowing when to harvest, knowing what parts of the crops are edible, how to get them, and how much seed to be saved for next season, and knowing how to properly rotate your crops so that the soil doesn't lose quality.<br /> Since there's also a lack of modern science that the Science skill can be applied to in that era, it stops the Science skill from becoming practically useless.<br /> <br /> I also want to point out that Animal Ken is for socializing with animals. Training them, calming them, so on. Knowing what to feed them probably goes under Science. Treating them if they are wounded or suffers from illness is something for Medicine. A farmer should have at least one dot Animal Ken to not agitate their animals, but Science and Crafts/Survival (explained further down) is probably more important.<br /> <br /> Crafts is another important skill for building fences and maintaining tools. Crafts is also needed for smithing (for the tools) and pottery (containers for seeds and foods), but that's probably covered by people specializing in those areas.<br /> <br /> Butchering could possibly be done with Crafts, but it's also something that hunters do (at least field dressing) so Survival is probably a more fitting skill. Skill overlap is always a possibility, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T10:05:07-08:00","id":1008588,"title":"","content":"I would say the physical part of farming, ploughing the ground, sowing seeds, etc, would fall under crafts. Knowing what time to plant, what time to harvest, etc, could be Wits + Survival to feel the air changing and tap into those farmer's instincts. Intelligence + Science would involve testing the soil and other such modern scientific techniques that depending on the era you're playing in might not exist yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T10:06:58-08:00","id":1008591,"title":"","content":"I'd say most subsistence farmers are focused on Crafts with Animal Ken depending on how much they use animals.<br /> <br /> Science is important, but one of those things that would usually be shopped out to a few elders rather than common knowledge. If you look at a number of religions, they contain all of the agricultural science of their day and use religious norms to communicate best practices when it comes to things like planting and harvesting.<br /> <br /> Survival is also more supplemental (very important mind you, but still supplemental) to agriculture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T10:32:06-08:00","id":1008598,"title":"","content":"Crafts and Athletics; a little bit of Animal Ken for farmers handling the cattle herds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T11:29:24-08:00","id":1008624,"title":"","content":"Science would be my main figuring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T16:16:14-08:00","id":1008710,"title":"","content":"I think the issue is that while Science (esp. as described in Dark Eras) is clearly the Skill you'd roll to figure out/remember the rules of agriculture, any agrarian society turns that into a specialist job with someone that tells the farmers when the right time to do X is this year.<br /> <br /> If you're innovating, farming in new terrain without the help of experienced residents, or simply living away from any larger community, Science would clearly become more important. If you live in a farming community and the local priest reads the signs to announce when to start your planting you don't need to worry about learning it (aka take some Science dots).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}